d.3. Key Takeaways & Lessons Learned include the following questions:

1. What did the successful case do right?
•	Prioritized user experience by making the system intuitive and reliable.
•	Implemented strong verification and security measures, reducing fraud.
•	Engaged landlords, students, and universities, ensuring active participation.
•	Conducted pilot testing to refine the system before full-scale launch.
2. What went wrong in the failed case?
•	Lack of quality control, allowing fake and outdated listings.
•	No user support or fraud detection, making it easy for scams to occur.
•	Weak technical performance, leading to frequent crashes and poor functionality.
•	Poor marketing and adoption strategy, resulting in low visibility and trust.
3. How can future implementations avoid similar failures?
•	Prioritize Verification & Security: Implement strict listing verification to prevent fraud.Engage Stakeholders Early: Work closely with landlords, universities, and local authorities to ensure trusted listings.
•	User-Friendly Design & Testing: Conduct pilot testing, gather feedback, and fix usability issues before full-scale launch.
•	Strategic Marketing & Awareness: Use partnerships, social media campaigns, and targeted promotions to boost adoption.

e. Insights & recommendations

e.1. Best Practices for Successful Enterprise System Implementation
•	Thorough Needs Assessment & Stakeholder Engagement: Engage stakeholders early, conduct surveys, and gather feedback from users and landlords.
•	Systematic Verification & Security: Implement a strong listing verification process and ensure data protection.
•	User-Centered Design & Iterative Testing: Focus on an intuitive design and conduct pilot testing for continuous improvement.
•	Effective Marketing & Awareness Campaigns: Promote the platform via universities, social media, and local businesses to boost adoption.
•	Scalable Infrastructure & Future-Proofing: Ensure cloud-based, scalable infrastructure and integrate analytics for system optimization.

e.2. Strategies to Avoid Failure
•	Avoid Over-Reliance on Automation: Incorporate manual verification alongside automation to prevent fraud.
•	Address Technical Issues Early: Conduct stress tests and maintain system performance to prevent glitches.
•	Foster Strong Stakeholder Relationships: Actively engage landlords and local businesses to ensure reliable listings.
•	Listen to User Feedback: Regularly collect user feedback to improve the platform and fix issues.

e.3. Future Research Opportunities
•	AI for Enhanced Matching: Investigate AI algorithms for better property recommendations based on user preferences.
•	Blockchain for Trust: Explore blockchain for transparent transactions and landlord verification.
•	User Behavior Analysis & Personalization: Study user patterns to offer personalized experiences.
•	Sustainability in Boarding Houses: Research eco-friendly housing models and future market trends in student accommodations.





